<!-- Intro, 1.1 s at 60 fps, after the matchup locator. A light ignites on the
     seam between the team rows and the clock panel and splits into two leading
     edges that wipe the block open outward (in-out, 0.47 s): the rows to the
     left, the clock panel to the right. The content drifts outward behind the
     edges, the faded logos settle from 112%, and the scores, acronyms and clock
     text rise in letter by letter, outward from the seam. The team markers draw
     outward from the seam between the rows once the edge has passed, a trace
     is drawn round the shot clock cell and fades, the sponsor rises into its
     strip, and one specular sweep crosses the glass to finish. Everything reads
     by about 0.67 s. Every ease decelerates without overshoot. The first block
     restores what Outro and Hidden change. -->
